# `ch` = Chärjew dialect

`src/i18n/ch.json` is the **Chärjew (Çärjow) dialect of Turkmen** (Lebap / Türkmenabat).
Never copy a `tk.json` value into it.

Before writing or editing any `ch` value, **read and follow
`.claude/skills/charjew-translation/SKILL.md`** and its `glossary.md`. To see how
the file already renders a word:

```bash
node .claude/skills/charjew-translation/compare.mjs "<regex>" --dialect
```

`scripts/translations/add-translation-row.mjs` can only write standard Turkmen
into `ch.json`. Rewrite that value by hand right after running it.
